      "id": "a0",
      "text": "Ray Davis led the Homestake experiment that first measured solar neutrinos.",
      "label": "p1",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "text": "The Homestake detector used gallium as its target material.",
      "label": "p2",
      "factual": false,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "text": "The Homestake experiment detected roughly one-third of the electron neutrinos predicted by theory.",
      "label": "p3",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "a3",
      "text": "John Bahcall developed the standard solar model calculations of the expected neutrino flux.",
      "label": "p4",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "a4",
      "text": "Helioseismology measurements of the Sun's interior agreed closely with the standard solar model.",
      "label": "p5",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "a5",
      "text": "The Sudbury Neutrino Observatory used heavy water as its detection medium.",
      "label": "p6",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "a6",
      "text": "SNO's detector contained 1,000 tonnes of ordinary light water as its primary target.",
      "label": "p7",
      "factual": false,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "a7",
      "text": "SNO measured a neutral-current reaction that is equally sensitive to all three neutrino flavors.",
      "label": "p8",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "a8",
      "text": "The total flux of boron-8 solar neutrinos measured by SNO agreed with the standard solar model prediction.",
      "label": "p9",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "a9",
      "text": "SNO's count of boron-8 solar neutrinos of all flavors matched the number the standard solar model forecast.",
      "label": "p10",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "a10",
      "text": "The SNO collaboration's 2002 results ultimately determined that the solar neutrino deficit did not stem from an error in the standard solar model.",
      "label": "p11",
      "factual": true,
      "role": "claim",
      "pos": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "a11",
      "text": "The Nobel Committee concluded that SNO's measurements showed solar neutrinos change identity on their way to Earth.",
